    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c9aa15b3",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts four drag queens taking a selfie, with overlaid text reading \"maybe if you worked a bit we wouldn't have inequality.\" The scene juxtaposes the glamorous, high-energy presentation of drag performers with a cynical, economically deterministic message about inequality. The intent is to use the visual contrast to mock or dismiss the idea that systemic inequality can be solved by individual effort alone. While not explicitly targeting a specific protected group with hate, the meme's message is harmful because it oversimplifies complex social and economic issues, potentially undermining legitimate discussions about structural inequality and systemic barriers. It frames the struggle against inequality as a personal failure rather than a societal problem, which can be demoralizing and misleading. The meme may also be perceived as dismissive of the labor and resilience of marginalized communities, including those in the LGBTQ+ community who often face systemic barriers, thus carrying implicit harmful undertones.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8ecb0f5a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
